<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoninus Pius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">86–161</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoninus Pius was Roman emperor from 138 to 161, adopted heir of Hadrian and adoptive father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a>. His long reign was among the most peaceful in Roman history; he never left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> as emperor. The one major advance of the frontier was in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, where his governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-lollius-urbicus">Quintus Lollius Urbicus</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonine-wall">Antonine Wall</a> between the Forth and the Clyde.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius.jpg" alt="Antoninus Pius" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jebulon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoninus_Pius_bust_S2436_ancient_agora_museum_Athens.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
